              %li
                %a{:href => "#history"} History
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em strict 2-categories
            is the simplest generalization of that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            to the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-categories"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-categories
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} categorification
            of the concept of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with strict choice of structure morphisms.
          %p
            More concretely, a strict 2-category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+n-graph"} directed 2-graph
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal-
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            of adjacent 1-cells (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"}> 1-morphisms
            ) and 2-cells (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"}> 2-morphisms
            ), respectively, which is strictly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unital
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
            in both directions, and such that both types of composition are compatible (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interchange+law"}> interchange law
            ”).
          %p
            A quick way of making this precise, is to say that strict 2-categories are
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DefinitionStrictTwoCategories"} below
          %p
            The term
            %em 2-category
            implicitly refers to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shapes+for+higher+structures"} globular
            structure. By contrast,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double categories
            are based on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubes"} cubes
            instead. The two notions are closely related, however: every strict 2-category gives rise to several strict double categories, and every double category has several
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            2-categories.
          %p
            Notice that
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            is another term for
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+category"} 2-fold category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete
          %p
            (And similarly, strict globular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-categories
            may be identified with those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+category"} n-fold categories
            for which all cube faces “in one direction” are discrete. A similar statement for weak
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionStrictTwoCategories Strict 2-categories
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %em strict 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %em 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} category enriched over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            is regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            between them and equipped with the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            given by forming
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+categories"} product categories
          %h3#strict_2groupoids Strict 2-groupoids
          %p
            Similarly, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-groupoid"} strict 2-groupoid
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+groupoid"} groupoid enriched
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shapes+for+higher+structures"} globular
                strict 2-groupoid
          %p
            The category of strict 2-groupoids is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+modules"} crossed modules
            over groupoids. It is also equivalent to the category of (strict)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+groupoids"} double groupoids
            “with connections”.
          %p
            They are also special cases of strict globular omega-groupoids, and the category of these is equivalent to the category of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
          %h3#details Details
          %p
            Working out the meaning of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"}> Cat
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            (
            %a{:href => "#DefinitionStrictTwoCategories"}> above
            ), we find that a strict 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is given by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ob
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ob K
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c,\ldots
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-category"} hom-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(a,b)
                for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"}> identity morphisms
                    )
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a : \mathbf{1} \to K(a,a)
                %li
                  %p
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"}> composition
                    )
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi comp
                          %mo :
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo ,
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp : K(b,c) \times K(a,b) \to K(a,c)
              %p
                for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unitality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
                (as given at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %p
            As for ordinary (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            \-enriched)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in K(a,b)
            is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphism"} 1-morphism
            or
            %em 1-cell
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and written
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:a\to b
            as usual. But given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:a\to b
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:f\to g \in K(a,b)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
            or
            %em 2-cells
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            and written as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : f \Rightarrow g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(a,b)
            are by definition categories, 2-cells carry an associative and unital operation called
            = succeed "." do
              %em vertical composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_f
            given by the category structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(a,b)
          %p
            The functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            gives us an operation of
            %em horizontal
            composition on 2-cells. Functoriality of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            then says that given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : f \Rightarrow g : a\to b
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : f' \Rightarrow g' : b\to c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} comp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \comp(\beta,\alpha)
            is a 2-cell
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \alpha : f'f \Rightarrow g'g : a \to c
          %p
            We also have the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interchange+law"} interchange law
            (also called
            %em Godement law
            or
            = succeed "):" do
              %em middle 4 interchange law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            is a functor it commutes with composition in the hom-categories, so we have (writing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            as juxtaposition):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mo ′
                  %mi α
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\beta' \circ \beta)(\alpha' \circ \alpha) = (\beta' \alpha') \circ (\beta \alpha)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unitality
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            ensure that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            behaves just like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            on objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-categories"} hom-categories
            (i.e. 1-cells of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %h3#detailedDefn More details
          %p
            (See also the section below on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquicategories"} sesquicategories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} stuff and structure
            described below.)
          %p
            In even more detail, a strict
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            consists of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em stuff
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ob
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob K
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ob
                        %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob_K
                of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                    \-cells
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                and object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(a,b)
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_K(a,b)
                of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                or
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                  \-cells
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \to b
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon a \to b
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon a \to b
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(f,g)
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 Hom_K(f,g)
                of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                or
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g\colon a \to b
          %p
            that is equipped with the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a\colon a \to a
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \id_a\colon a \to a
            %li
              %p
                for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon a \to b
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon b \to c
                %em composite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ;
